{
 "_comment": [
  "Sourcing data for the BOM: board.py attaches these as symbol fields (Manufacturer, MPN,",
  "LCSC, Assembly, Desc, Socket_Manufacturer, Socket_MPN) and fab_export.py turns them into",
  "the JLCPCB and PCBWay assembly files.  Keys in by_value are 'value|footprint' (footprint",
  "may be '*'); by_ref overrides per reference.",
  "assembly: pcba      = the assembler buys and mounts it",
  "          customer  = we supply and mount it ourselves (not in the assembly BOM/CPL)",
  "          socket    = the assembler mounts the SOCKET (socket.* fields); the chip is a",
  "                      separate BOM line, supplied by chip_supply (customer | pcba, inserted",
  "                      after assembly)",
  "          dnp       = not placed at all",
  "verify: true marks a part number written from memory that has not been checked against a",
  "distributor listing yet; fab_export.py lists them.  lcsc is only needed for JLCPCB and may",
  "be left out: JLCPCB's BOM tool matches basic passives by value and footprint."
 ],
